The Flaming Lady answered my questions without trouble.
I think the God of Fire did not foresee this kind of interaction between her and other beings and did not think to control it.
Part of the creatures of the Heart of Fire were made from lava and volcanic rock. The other part was made from the bodies of invading adventurers who, as punishment, were turned into monsters by the God of Fire to serve as slaves and suffer for all eternity.
It was said that the God of Fire was responsible for every flame in the world. It seems he was not sociable with the other gods and had problems with Midranda.
When I asked why, the Flaming Lady went limp and collapsed to the ground. And she did not say another word.

I need to take it all in. Please, come back later.
